  "scope": "Complete Borel univalent selection for every Lebesgue-measurable source set: the Borel subset lies in A and the actual positive-Jacobian locus, f is injective on it, and its image misses only a Hausdorff m-null subset of f(A). Prove countable Borel image-disjointification selection, its empty-family case and exact preservation of the selected Borel rank image. Identify positive Jacobian with injective differential locus. The numbered statement retains m<=n; the supporting theorem allows arbitrary ambient dimensions. Two regressions cover zero-dimensional source positive Jacobian and selection from an empty family.",
